# An app docks; it is never installed: the worked ibuki example
# (theory/IBUKI.md). The root states the ceiling and the providers, `blue lock`
# proves the join of every package's floor fits under them and records the
# proof, and `blue bundle` seals the program and that record into an appliance
# that takes no flags.
#
#   blue lock .                      verify the lattice, write the record
#   blue test app.b                  the app's tests, the breach proof included
#   blue run app.b                   held to the record: the clock is stepped
#   blue bundle app.b --runner "$(command -v blue-appliance)" -o pacer
#
# The ceiling is pure: no host capability reaches the host. The clock is
# virtualized to a stepped provider, so the Flash bucket the app paces reads a
# clock that starts at 0 and advances 5 ms a reading, and every run prints the
# same lines. Add a host word outside a test block and `blue lock` refuses,
# naming the package and the capability.
#
# A floor counts a whole package: ibuki uses shomei's hashes, and shomei also
# holds `random`, so shomei's floor names entropy though nothing here calls it.
# The seeded provider, scoped to shomei, answers that floor without the host.
package("ibuki-docking", "0.1.0")

allow([])
virtualize(:clock, {using: :deterministic_stepped, at_ms: 0, step_ms: 5})
virtualize(:entropy, {using: :seeded_prng, seed: "ibuki-docking", for: %w[shomei]})

check("app", "app.b", ["Bluefile.lock"])
app("pacer", "app.b")
